=== accusation ===
The file is not a feeling. It is the set of claims that survive contact with one another.

Before the final page, you write the argument in plain language. Plain language is unforgiving. It does not let a missing link hide behind a dramatic noun.

* [Review the full chain]
    -> case_review
* [Submit the case]
    ~ evaluate_accusation("arin")
    -> consequence
* [Keep the case open]
    You leave the final line blank. That is a conclusion, too.
    -> END

=== case_review ===
The case can be written four ways. Only one of them explains the evidence without asking the evidence to do a different job.

* [Who]
    Arin bought the aconite. The blue tape fiber places his injured hand against the concealed underside of the lid.
    -> case_review
* [Why]
    Eli's scheduled article and attached invoices exposed Arin's paid reviews. That is motive. The fiber still has to supply contact.
    -> case_review
* [How]
    Aconite appears beneath the lid. The rim was wiped, but residue and one blue adhesive fiber remained where an ordinary touch would not leave them.
    -> case_review
* [When]
    Arin's borrowed tag opens the service door before the camera gap and records his exit at 19:25. Eli drank at 19:24 and died between 19:25 and 19:28.
    -> case_review
* [What does not follow]
    Mira's false departure does not prove murder. Sasha's debt, Jo's camera mistake, and Dan's theft do not prove murder either. Their exclusion records explain those lies without forcing them into the poisoning.
    -> case_review
* [Submit the reviewed case]
    -> final_hearing

=== final_hearing ===
There is no courtroom in Café Lantern. There is a counter, a back booth, and five people pretending not to listen.

You read the argument aloud because silent logic is easy to edit after the fact.

Mira was present at 19:22 despite saying she had left at 19:10. That contradiction establishes a false statement. Her later account places Arin beside Eli's booth at 19:23, but a witness alone does not establish the method.

The camera was offline from 19:18 to 19:29. That establishes an opportunity shared by anyone who could reach the booth. It does not establish an actor.

Eli drank at 19:24 and died between 19:25 and 19:28 from aconite in his drink. That establishes a method and a window. It does not establish a purchaser.

Arin bought aconite at 19:04 and said he bought cough drops. That establishes a false statement and a connection to the poison. It does not, by itself, establish that he used it.

The cup lid was wiped and still carried residue. A blue adhesive fiber beneath it matches the tape on Arin's cut finger. Together they establish contact with the concealed surface and an attempt to remove a trace.

Eli's scheduled article and invoices establish Arin's reason to stop him. The service-door log places Arin's borrowed tag on the route before the cup was altered and records an exit at 19:25.

The conclusion arrives only when the evidence is joined. The voicemail keeps Sasha outside. The till log keeps Jo at the register. The delivery records take Dan away before Eli drinks. Mira's second statement explains her lie and places Arin by the booth. Their suspicious facts survive, but their murder theories do not.

* [Read the conclusion]
    You accuse Arin Ko of poisoning Eli Venn's iced americano during the camera outage, then wiping the lid and lying about the pharmacy purchase.
    # outcome:conviction
    -> END
* [Read the caution]
    The case remains a case only while its links are visible. Remove the pharmacy purchase and the conclusion becomes a possibility. Remove the lid and the link becomes weaker. Remove the death window and the timing floats.
    -> END

=== consequence ===
The room does not become brighter when the argument is complete. The cup is still a cup. The receipt is still a narrow strip of paper that curled at one end.

What changes is the order. Arin's purchase comes before the blind spot. His borrowed tag brackets the route through the café. The hidden fiber joins his hand to the wiped lid. The exclusions move Mira, Jo, Sasha, and Dan out of the sequence without pretending they told the truth.

You think about the difference between noticing a person and proving a sequence. The first can happen in a second. The second takes a file, a witness, and the patience to leave a gap visible.

* [Close the report]
    -> END
